{
  "_readme": "DIV-4 share strip, one fixture both suites read. `document`: the member door's DIV-4 document (runtime pane on); `laneOff`: the same script with the runtime pane off; `copy`: runtime_definitions.without_run_reads(document), what a share preview and an installed copy carry. pytest: tests/test_share_strips_run_reads.py (copy == the server's strip). vitest: memberPane/shareStripCopy.test.js (document == the door's; copy draws host colours with no stale disclosure).",
  "source": "//@version=5\nindicator(\"div4 rail\", overlay = true)\nlen = input.int(3, \"Len\")\nhi = ta.highest(high, len)[1]\nlo = ta.lowest(low, len)[1]\nvar int trend = 1\ntrend := close > hi ? 1 : close < lo ? -1 : trend\nup = trend == 1 and trend[1] == -1\ndn = trend == -1 and trend[1] == 1\nb = ta.barssince(up)\ns = ta.barssince(dn)\nplot(ta.sma(close, len), \"c\")\nbarcolor(b < s ? color.green : b > s ? color.red : na, title = \"bc\")\n",
